# VibeTalk env template — NAMES ONLY, no values. Copy to .env for local dev.
#
# BUILD-TIME vs RUNTIME — read this before touching any var (audit-2 M74):
# - RUNTIME vars (no VITE_ prefix) are read from process.env on EVERY
#   request by server functions. Change the value in the host
#   dashboard and the server picks it up — no code rebuild needed
#   (the host may still need a redeploy to apply a dashboard change).
# - BUILD-TIME vars (VITE_ prefix) are INLINED into the client JS
#   bundle at build time (vite `define` / import.meta.env). Changing
#   the value in a dashboard does NOTHING until the next build +
#   redeploy — the running bundle keeps the old value baked in.
#
# DRIFT RULE: SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_URL (+ VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID)
# MUST point at the SAME Supabase project. If they drift apart (e.g.
# server vars moved to a new project but the client bundle was never
# rebuilt), auth tokens minted by one project fail validation on the
# other — and the failure looks like an auth bug, not config drift.
# The app detects this at runtime (getServerSupabaseConfig +
# detectSupabaseDrift) and toasts a "Supabase config drift" warning.
#
# Secrets (SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY) are NEVER put here
# or in any checked-in file. They live ONLY in:
#   Cloudflare -> Worker "hc" secrets (wrangler secret put)
#   Vercel     -> project "vibetalk" dashboard env vars
# Without them, server fns throw "Missing Supabase environment variable(s)"
# and push is off. See AGENTS.md "Secrets" section.

# --- RUNTIME (server; read per request) ---
# Supabase project the SERVER talks to (admin + auth validation).
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# VAPID keypair the server SIGNS pushes with. Must match the client's
# baked VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY (same keypair) — see M72 note below.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT: sender-contact URL in the VAPID `sub` claim. Defaults to
# the Cloudflare origin when unset (M72). Vercel: set to
# https://vibetalk-one.vercel.app so Vercel-sent pushes identify correctly.
VAPID_SUBJECT=

# --- BUILD-TIME (client; baked into the JS bundle at build) ---
# Supabase project the BROWSER talks to (auth + PostgREST). Must be the
# SAME project as SUPABASE_URL above. A dashboard change here needs a
# rebuild + redeploy to take effect.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_PROJECT_ID=
# Audit-2 M72: VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY and VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY MUST be
# IDENTICAL (same keypair) and rotated TOGETHER. The server key is
# authoritative — the client resolves it server-first via
# getVapidPublicKey and only falls back to the VITE_ var when the
# server fn is unavailable. A drifted pair used to 401 every push.
VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# TURN relay for WebRTC calls (client-only; read at call time).
# ⚠️ WARNING: VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL ships inside the PUBLIC JS bundle —
# anyone can extract it and use your relay. Use ONLY a restricted /
# rate-limited TURN credential here (e.g. OpenRelay's public one),
# never a privileged or long-lived credential. All three vars must be
# set together — setting only some runs STUN-only with a console warning
# (see getTurnStatus / warnIfTurnPartial in src/lib/calls.ts).
# Ephemeral server-minted TURN credentials (time-limited, preferred)
# are NOT yet implemented — the static credential remains until then.
VITE_TURN_URLS=
VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=

# Secrets — dashboards only, NEVER in this file:
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
